WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.510
- I loved what y'all were
talking about in the video too.

00:00:01.510 --> 00:00:02.343
I think that about a song.

00:00:02.343 --> 00:00:03.176
If you can't break it down

00:00:03.176 --> 00:00:05.300
with just a piano or just a guitar,

00:00:05.300 --> 00:00:06.170
then it's not a great song.

00:00:06.170 --> 00:00:07.720
You're the most magical songwriter.

00:00:07.720 --> 00:00:08.810
- And when we've worked together,

00:00:08.810 --> 00:00:09.740
I mean it's always like,

00:00:09.740 --> 00:00:13.750
can we make this work without
all the bells and whistles?

00:00:13.750 --> 00:00:14.583
And if you can,

00:00:14.583 --> 00:00:16.240
then you can put all that stuff on it

00:00:16.240 --> 00:00:17.130
and the song really works.

00:00:17.130 --> 00:00:17.963
- But, if you can't,

00:00:17.963 --> 00:00:18.796
it's not really what it's supposed to be.

00:00:18.796 --> 00:00:19.770
- Exactly, exactly.
- I agree.

00:00:19.770 --> 00:00:21.890
We do non-kid stuff too though y'all.

00:00:21.890 --> 00:00:24.390
We've lost a lot, I've lost a lot,

00:00:24.390 --> 00:00:25.740
of money in Vegas with you.

00:00:26.580 --> 00:00:27.910
But, we won a lot one time!

00:00:27.910 --> 00:00:28.997
- I know.
- And we've done duets.

00:00:28.997 --> 00:00:30.504
- But, that one time when we won,

00:00:30.504 --> 00:00:32.600
we have been trying...

00:00:32.600 --> 00:00:33.433
- The one time we won,

00:00:33.433 --> 00:00:34.270
we won...
- But, it was like...

00:00:34.270 --> 00:00:35.110
- What game are you playing?

00:00:35.110 --> 00:00:35.993
Craps?

00:00:35.993 --> 00:00:37.310
- We were playing, well
we played, 3-card poker,

00:00:37.310 --> 00:00:38.340
we played slots...
- Slots.

00:00:38.340 --> 00:00:39.920
- Remember at that 3-card poker table?

00:00:39.920 --> 00:00:41.970
Where that person came up to you and said

00:00:42.810 --> 00:00:43.643
the dealer was like,

00:00:43.643 --> 00:00:46.760
oh I love So Small so much
it's my favorite song.

00:00:46.760 --> 00:00:47.593
- Yeah, Carrie Underwood.

00:00:47.593 --> 00:00:49.491
I was like, I'm not Carrie Underwood.

00:00:49.491 --> 00:00:51.490
Yeah.
(laughs)

00:00:51.490 --> 00:00:52.323
- I mean, literally,

00:00:52.323 --> 00:00:53.510
I'm so complimented by it

00:00:53.510 --> 00:00:54.790
because she's like super hot and thin

00:00:54.790 --> 00:00:56.145
so I'm like, maybe I'll just rock it.

00:00:56.145 --> 00:00:57.290
Maybe I'll just be like, yes, thank you.

00:00:57.290 --> 00:00:58.752
- Well, of course, I'm behind her going,

00:00:58.752 --> 00:01:00.742
hey dumb ass, that's Kelly Clarkson.

00:01:00.742 --> 00:01:02.241
(laughs)

00:01:02.241 --> 00:01:03.750
- Like, huge star!
- I loved it though.

00:01:03.750 --> 00:01:04.583
I loved it.

00:01:04.583 --> 00:01:05.930
Now, we also karaoke as well.

00:01:05.930 --> 00:01:07.030
We have karaoked quite a bit.

00:01:07.030 --> 00:01:10.060
- I have to tell the
karaoke story about you.

00:01:10.060 --> 00:01:13.127
- Okay, is it daytime appropriate?

00:01:13.127 --> 00:01:14.690
- It is, well I mean, look.

00:01:14.690 --> 00:01:15.720
I don't know for sure

00:01:15.720 --> 00:01:18.020
if anything we've done
is daytime appropriate.

00:01:18.960 --> 00:01:21.070
So, we would go karaokeing in Nashville,

00:01:21.070 --> 00:01:22.730
which I know you have an
actual connection with.

00:01:22.730 --> 00:01:23.563
- Yes.

00:01:23.563 --> 00:01:24.997
- They should come karaokeing sometime.

00:01:24.997 --> 00:01:25.830
- Okay.

00:01:25.830 --> 00:01:29.660
- But, this woman,
she's up there in a wig.

00:01:29.660 --> 00:01:31.350
She wears this crazy Mohawk wig.

00:01:31.350 --> 00:01:32.183
- I love wigs.

00:01:32.183 --> 00:01:33.016
- And she's singing.

00:01:33.016 --> 00:01:36.260
I think you were singing
Ice Ice Baby in my mind.

00:01:36.260 --> 00:01:38.506
- Maybe with Donovan then.
- Yeah, probably.

00:01:38.506 --> 00:01:39.339
- Yeah, that's her song, that's her go-to.

00:01:39.339 --> 00:01:41.120
- And, yeah, with Ashley Donovan

00:01:41.120 --> 00:01:42.617
and this woman goes,

00:01:42.617 --> 00:01:45.830
that girl reminds me so
much of Kelly Clarkson.

00:01:45.830 --> 00:01:47.895
I mean, she's no Kelly Clarkson.

00:01:47.895 --> 00:01:49.627
(laughs)

00:01:49.627 --> 00:01:51.240
But, she reminds me of her.

00:01:51.240 --> 00:01:53.130
It was so fun.
- Well, I was probably d-runk,

00:01:53.130 --> 00:01:54.233
so I probably wasn't.

00:01:55.250 --> 00:01:56.900
- No, that was awesome.

00:01:56.900 --> 00:01:58.238
- It is the most fun place
to go karaokeing though.

00:01:58.238 --> 00:01:59.370
All the honky tonks,

00:01:59.370 --> 00:02:00.203
there's bars right down there.

00:02:00.203 --> 00:02:01.510
- Well then everybody can really sing.

00:02:01.510 --> 00:02:03.410
- I know, but it's good
when the bad ones get up.

00:02:03.410 --> 00:02:04.243
- I know, right?

00:02:04.243 --> 00:02:05.076
- Yeah, those are the fun ones.

00:02:05.076 --> 00:02:05.909
- Right, that's like
when I get up and sing.

00:02:05.909 --> 00:02:06.742
- Yeah, it's like Rudy.

00:02:06.742 --> 00:02:07.575
You're like, you can do it!

00:02:07.575 --> 00:02:08.408
- Do it Rudy!

00:02:08.408 --> 00:02:09.241
(laughs)

00:02:09.241 --> 00:02:10.100
- So, how is your mom?

00:02:10.100 --> 00:02:11.320
I saw her at that Dallas show.

00:02:11.320 --> 00:02:12.310
I didn't know this,

00:02:12.310 --> 00:02:14.040
but I read your pre-interview.

00:02:14.040 --> 00:02:15.490
I didn't know that you told your mom,

00:02:15.490 --> 00:02:17.160
whatever you do, don't
mention American Idol.

00:02:17.160 --> 00:02:18.240
Which, I don't know why
you would have done that.

00:02:18.240 --> 00:02:19.073
I don't care.

00:02:19.073 --> 00:02:21.607
But, it was the first
thing she said to me!

00:02:21.607 --> 00:02:23.500
- So, I have this little show.

00:02:23.500 --> 00:02:24.430
I'm doing this songwriter show.

00:02:24.430 --> 00:02:27.000
I mean, this is 2006?
- This is a long time ago.

00:02:27.000 --> 00:02:27.877
- I mean, that's a long time ago.

00:02:27.877 --> 00:02:28.710
- Yeah.

00:02:28.710 --> 00:02:29.960
- And Kelly was going to come.

00:02:29.960 --> 00:02:31.990
Now, this is a small room of people

00:02:31.990 --> 00:02:33.250
and my mom was like,

00:02:33.250 --> 00:02:34.083
I just want to meet Kelly.

00:02:34.083 --> 00:02:34.916
I just want to meet Kelly.

00:02:34.916 --> 00:02:35.749
And I said, look,

00:02:35.749 --> 00:02:36.582
I'm going to introduce you to Kelly.

00:02:36.582 --> 00:02:37.710
I don't even really know her that well,

00:02:37.710 --> 00:02:40.870
but I do know that all she ever
hears about is American Idol

00:02:40.870 --> 00:02:41.958
so just don't mention that.

00:02:41.958 --> 00:02:42.830
- Which I didn't care.

00:02:42.830 --> 00:02:43.810
- I know, but I didn't know you

00:02:43.810 --> 00:02:45.100
and my mom said,

00:02:45.100 --> 00:02:46.240
oh I would never do that.

00:02:46.240 --> 00:02:48.440
Okay, so then I say,

00:02:48.440 --> 00:02:50.740
mom this is Kelly, and she goes,

00:02:50.740 --> 00:02:52.751
we voted for you every week.

00:02:52.751 --> 00:02:55.481
(laughs)

00:02:55.481 --> 00:02:57.248
It was the first thing.

00:02:57.248 --> 00:02:58.081
(applause)

00:02:58.081 --> 00:02:58.914
- That's what moms are for.
- That's exactly right.

00:02:58.914 --> 00:03:00.426
- To embarrass the heck out of you.

00:03:00.426 --> 00:03:01.576
- I love it. I love it.

